# MNT-2: keep the docker build context to actual sources.
#
# The Dockerfiles now `COPY . .` (see deployment/docker/*.Dockerfile for why). In CI that is a fresh
# checkout and harmless, but a local `docker build` would otherwise ship every target/ directory,
# the vendored node_modules, ~100MB of Playwright output and whatever is in scratch/ — slow, and
# worse, host-built target/ dirs landing in the image build where they can shadow a clean compile.
#
# Mirrors .gitignore; anything ignored there has no business in an image build either.

# Build output
target/
bin/
*.class

# Vendored / generated
node_modules/
playwright-output/
scratch/

# Local tooling and state
.git/
.github/
.idea/
*.iml
*.log

# Deliberately NOT excluded, because both are build inputs and excluding them produces an image
# that builds clean and fails at runtime:
#   *.md   — ai-qa-os-agents/src/main/resources/prompts/*.md are the MOD-3 agent prompts, packaged
#            into the jar and loaded at run time. Excluding them yields an agent with no prompts.
#   deployment/migration — the gateway and dashboard copy those SQL files onto their classpath as a
#            build resource (ADR-024), so Flyway would find no migrations.
